<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH DELAY FOKKER BRIEFING.</title>
<headline>DUTCH DELAY FOKKER BRIEFING.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch economic affairs ministry said on Thursday that a briefing on bankrupt planemaker Fokker NV, earlier planned for 1130 GMT, was postponed until further notice.</p>
<p>The ministry said the briefing was on hold and another statement would be issued later in the day.</p>
<p>The Dutch and Malaysian governments, Stork, which owns Fokker Aviation, Fokker administrators and Andre Deleye, chairman of Dutch industrial group Begemann NV, have been negotiating for weeks in an attempt to salvage something from the company that was declared bankrupt last March.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
